From 637af2350afc9a3ec9b585c922eb7a8120c439f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 08:46:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] WIP mmb: per-arch tuning defaults (mmb_arch_cfg) + the
 dense geometry as a per-arch constant
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

S11 of wip/mmb-general/gfx1201-porting.md (§7 point 3).  Host-side only.

Every mmb_* tunable was env-only with a hard-coded gfx1151 value, so no arch
could differ without a wall of env vars -- which also made profiler runs hard
to trust (the plan's §12.5 env-flakiness note: the env gates are lazy getenvs
and rocprofv3 cannot see them).  There is now one table:

  struct mmb_arch_cfg { min_t, glu_thresh, routed_thresh, tall_mode, tiny_m,
                        tiny_tt, f32split_mode, f32split_min_k, f32split_min_m,
                        cache_max, shadow_mode, shadow_cap_mb, iq3xxs_glu,
                        hc16, down16, gatemix, blk16, res16, glu, bf16w,
                        dense_geom };

selected once from ggml_cuda_info().devices[0].cc by mmb_arch_defaults(cc),
with the existing env var kept as the override on every accessor.  The RDNA4
row carries only measured values (the S10 dense geometry); every other field
keeps the gfx1151 value, i.e. the pre-S11 behaviour, with a TODO(S12) marking
the constants that still need a per-arch measurement (routed/GLU thresholds,
tall/tiny-M, f32split, cache).

The dense geometry also stops being an inline GGML_CUDA_CC_IS_RDNA4 test in the
dispatch and becomes c.dense_geom (enum: MMB_GEOM_GFX11_SPLIT / MMB_GEOM_R4_256x128),
so the arch policy for it is visible in the same table as everything else.

New diagnostic: GGML_CUDA_MMB_CFG=1 (or MMB_LOG=1) prints the resolved config
once, e.g.

  MMB_CFG cc=0x1001201 dense_geom=1 min_t=512 glu_thresh=32 routed_thresh=32
  tall=2 tiny_m=1/1 f32split=1(min_m=128,min_k=0) cache=4 shadow=0/6144MB
  hc16=0 down16=0 gatemix=0 blk16=0 res16=0 glu=1 bf16w=1 iq3xxs_glu=0

so a profiler run can record what was actually used without env vars.

Verified: same-seed greedy hash 42cdf36d0633 unchanged (also with a threshold
override in effect); the gfx1151 device asm kernel set is byte-unchanged (90
kernels, 0 differing instructions -- this change is host-only); and the 27B
UD-IQ3_S interleaved r=5 win is preserved (+0.45 % pp8192 / +0.46 % pp32768,
S10 measured +0.52/+0.46).
